","The definition of whole body oxygen delivery is the rate at which oxygen is delivered to all tissues in the body. It is a measure of the body's ability to provide oxygen to the body's cells, which are essential for energy production and overall health.

Oxygen delivery is influenced by several factors, including oxygen consumption, blood volume, and the efficiency of oxygen transport. When oxygen delivery is insufficient to match oxygen consumption, the body can become damaged by hypoxia (oxygen deficiency).

Oxygen delivery is calculated using the following formula:

Oxygen Delivery (OD) = Oxygen Consumption (VO2) + Oxygen Reserve (OS)

