The entropy change (\(\Delta S\)) for a reaction is calculated using the following equation:

\[
\Delta S = \Sigma S_{\text{products}} - \Sigma S_{\text{reactants}}
\]

For the given reaction:

\[
2 \text{PbS(s)} + 3 \text{O}_2(g) \rightarrow 2 \text{PbO(s)} + 2 \text{SO}_2(g)
\]

Substituting the molar entropies:

\[
\Delta S = [2 \times 66.5 + 2 \times 248.2] - [2 \times 91.2 + 3 \times 205.1]
\]

