","When Grignard reagents react with carbon dioxide (CO₂), the primary product is a **carboxylic acid**. This occurs because the Grignard reagent attacks the carbonyl carbon of CO₂, forming an enolate intermediate, which is then protonated by water (or another proton source) to yield the carboxylic acid.  

