","When \( \text{H}_2\text{S} \) gas is passed into a mixture of \( \text{Mn}^{2+}, \text{Ni}^{2+}, \text{Cu}^{2+}, \) and \( \text{Hg}^{2+} \) ions in an acidified aqueous solution, the sulfides that precipitate are determined by the solubility product (\( K_{sp} \)) of their corresponding sulfides. The \( K_{sp} \) values for the sulfides are as follows:  
