Now, we can plug these values into the equation:

ΔH = -392 kJ/mol - (-340 kJ/mol) - 762 kJ/mol

ΔH = -392 kJ/mol + 340 kJ/mol - 762 kJ/mol

ΔH = -714 kJ/mol

So, the standard enthalpy change for the reaction between [Fe(H2O)6]2+ and 2Cl- ions to produce [FeCl4]2- complex ion is -714 kJ/mol.
