","The reaction in which toluene is oxidized to benzaldehyde using chromyl chloride is known as the **Swwartz reaction** (or **Swwartz oxidation*)**.  

\[
\text{Toluene} + \text{CrCl}_3 + \text{H}_2\text{O} \rightarrow \text{Benzaldehyde} + \text{CrCl}_4 + \text{HCl}
\]

**Key points:**  
- Chromyl chloride (CrCl$_3$) is the oxidizing agent.  
- The reaction is typically carried out in anhydrous acetic anhydride (AcOH) and phosphorus pentoxide (P}_2\text{O}_5\) to prevent the formation of benzaldehyde oxide (a unstable intermediate).  
- The reaction is selective for the oxidation of aromatic rings to aldehydes, preventing further oxidation to benzoic acid.  

Thus, the correct answer is $\boxed{\text{Schwartz reaction}}$.",ground_truth_similarity,"# Task Description
