\[
\nabla f(x^*) (y - x^*) = \lim_{t \to 0} \frac{f(x^* + t(y - x^-)) - f(x^*)}{t}.
\]
Since $f$ is convex, the derivative at $x^*$ is positive, so:
\[
\nabla f(x^*) (y - x^*) \geq 0.
\]
For any $y \in \mathcal{U}$, we have:
\[
\frac{f(y) - f(x^*)}{\lVert y - x^* \rVert} \geq \frac{\nabla f(x^*) (y - x^-)}{\lVert y - x^* \rVert}.
\]
Since $\nabla f(x^*) (y - x^*) \geq 0$, we have:
\[
\frac{f(y) - f(x^*)}{\lVert y - x^-\rVert} \geq \frac{\nabla f(x^*) (y - x^-)}{\lVert y - x^-\rVert}.
\]
However, this is not sufficient to show the quermim property. Instead, we use the Fréchet derivative to show that:
\[
\lim_{y \to x^*, y \in \mathcal{U}} \frac{f(y) - f(x^*)}{\lVert y - x^-\rVert} \geq 0.
\]
