","The magnetic field strength \( B \) at the center of a circular coil is given by the formula:
\[
B = \frac{2\pi \mu_0 N I}{2r} = \frac{\mu_0 N I}{r}
\]
where:
- \( I \) is the current in the coil (1 A)
- \( N \) is the number of turns (100)
- \( r \) is the radius of the coil (0.2 m)
- \( \mu_0 \) is the permeability of free space, which is \( 4\pi \times 10^{-7} \, \text{T·m/A} \).

Substituting the values:
\[
B = \frac{(4\pi \times 10^{-7} \, \text{T·m/A}) \times 100 \times 1 \, \text{A}}{0.2 \, \text{m}} = 2\pi \times 10^{-5} \, \text{T}
\]
Thus, the magnetic field strength at the center of the coil is:
\[
B = 2\pi \times 10^{-5} \, \text{T} \approx 6.28 \times 10^{-5} \, \text{T}
\]

Thus, the magnetic field strength at the center of the circular coil is \(\boxed{6.28 \times 10^{-5} \, \text{T}}\).",relevance,"# Task Description
