<USER_REQUEST>
A cylinder contains 2 moles of an ideal gas at an initial pressure of 2 atm and an initial volume of 4L. The gas expands isothermally until its volume becomes 8L. Calculate the work done by the gas during the expansion process.
</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
For an isothermal expansion of an ideal gas, the work done by the gas is given by:  
\[
W = nRT \ln \left( \frac{V_f}{V_i} \right)
\]  
where \( n = 2 \) moles, \( R = 8.314 \, \text{J/mol·K} \), \( T = 300 \, \text{K} \), \( V_f = 8 \, \text{L} \), and \( V_i = 4 \, \text{L} \).  

Substituting the values:  
\[
W = 2 \times 8.314 \times 300 \times \ln \left( \frac{8}{4} \right)
\]  
\[
W = 4988.4 \times \ln 2
\]  
\[
W \approx 4988.4 \times 0.693
\]  
\[
W \approx 3460. \, \text{J}
\]  

Thus, the work done by the gas during the expansion process is \(\boxed{3460 \, \text{J}}\).
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

