   Vapour density (V.D.) = Molar mass / (760 mm Hg / 101.325 mm Hg)  
   V.D. = Molar mass / (1 atm)  
   Given V.D. = 25.67, so Molar mass = 25.67 × 22.414 (1 atm) = 573.2 g/mol  
   (Note: The molar mass of N₂O₄ is 120 g/mol, but the given vapour density is for the mixture of N₂O₄ and NO₂. The correct molar mass of the mixture is calculated using the given vapour density.)

3. **Relate vapour density to molar mass of the mixture**:  
