The closed-loop gain \( A_{vf} \) is given by:
\[
A_{vf} = \frac{A_v}{1 - m_v}
\]

Substituting the given values:
\[
A_{vf} = \frac{100}{1 - 0.1} = \frac{100}{0.9} \approx 111.11
\]

The gain \( A_v \) decreases by 6 dB, which means the new gain is:
\[
A_v' = 100 \times 10^{-6/10} = 100 \times 0.1 = 10
\]

The new closed-loop gain \( A_{vf}' \) is:
\[
A_{vf}' = \frac{A_v'}{1 - m_v} = \frac{10}{1 - 0.1} = \frac{10}{0.9} \approx 11.11
\]

The percentage change in the closed-loop gain is:
\[
