","The number of lines per meter is \( 800 \times 10^3 = 8 \times 10^5 \text{ lines/meter} \). The number of lines per meter is \( n = 8 \times 10^5 \). The wavelength is \( \lambda = 600 \text{ nm} = 600 \times 10^{-9} \text{ m} \). The distance to the screen is \( d = 1.5 \text{ m} \). The order is \( m = 3 \).

The condition for diffraction grations is:
\[
n \lambda \sin \theta = m \lambda
\]
Solving for \( \sin \theta \):
\[
\sin \theta = \frac{m}{n}
