<start_of_turn>model
","1. **Compression Ratio (R)**:
   The efficiency of the Otto cycle is given by:
   \[
   \eta = 1 - \frac{1}{R^k}
   \]
   where \( \eta = 0.56 \) (56%), \( R = \frac{P_{\text{max}}}{P_{\text{low}}} \) (compression ratio), and \( k = 1.4 \) (isentropic constant for air).

   Solving for \( R \):
   \[
   0.56 = 1 - \frac{1}{R^{1.4}}
   \]
   \[
   \frac{1}{R^{1.4}} = 1 - 0.56 = 0.44
   \]
   \[
   R^{1.4} = \frac{1}{0.44} \approx 2.27
   \]
   \[
   R = 2.27^{1/1.4} \approx 1.55
   \]
   Thus, the compression ratio is \(\boxed{1.55}\).

2. **Work Done per kg of Air (W_{\text{out}})**:
   The efficiency is also given by:
   \[
   \eta = \frac{W_{\text{out}}}{Q_{\text{in}}} = frac{Q_{\text{in}} - Q_{\text{reject}}}{Q_{\text{in}}} = 1 - \frac{Q_{\text{reject}}}{Q_{\text{in}}}
   \]
   Given \( Q_{\text{reject}} = 544 \, \text{kJ/kg} \), and \( \eta = 0.56 \):
   \[
   0.56 = 1 - \frac{544}{Q_{\text{in}}}
   \]
   \[
   \frac{544}{Q_{\text{in}}} = 1 - 0.56 = 0.44
   \]
   \[
   Q_{\text{in}} = \frac{544}{0.44} \approx 1231 \, \text{kJ/kg}
   \]
   The work done per kg of air is:
   \[
   W_{\text{out}} = Q_{\text{in}} - Q_{\text{reject}} = 1231 - 544 = 687 \, \text{kJ/kg}
   \]
   Thus, the work done per kg of air is \(\boxed{687 \, \text{kJ/kg}}\).

3. **Pressure and Temperature at the End of Compression (P_{\text{max}}, T_{\text{max}})**:
